d (integration unmerged, eco grep 0); L4 blocked (no benchmark referee row).", "run_artifacts": ["docs/board_audit/m18144/evidence_snapshot/artifacts_orig/results.json", "docs/board_audit/m18144/evidence_snapshot/artifacts_orig/fused_kernel_selector.png", "docs/board_audit/m18144/evidence_snapshot/artifacts_repro/results.json"], "external_anchor": "lbmpy 2.0 + pystencils 2.0 installed and imported (xval/lbmpy_reference.py:44-47), JIT-compiled C kernel executed on numpy fields; selector semantics read from LBMConfig.kernel_type at runtime (zero hand-copied constants). Cross-check to round-off 1.1e-16..1.8e-15. But external anchor != benchmark referee row (see benchmark note).", "integration_callers": "NONE on main: grep -rl ''fused_kernel_selector|collide_stream_bgk'' /root/tensor-ecosystem/TensorLBM -> 0 files; the only call site is the UNCOMMITTED worktree diff snapshot docs/board_audit/m18144/evidence_snapshot/channel_integration.patch (52 lines: ChannelConfig.kernel_type -> collide_stream_bgk in run_channel). Auditor did run both kernel_type arms through sediment.channel (200 steps): u_star 0.008730409936128732 identical, rel=0.0, profile_rel_err identical. L3 NOT claimed because the gate''s machine criterion (grep on the ecosystem repo) is unsatisfiable while the code is untracked.", "entry_note": "CLI: bench --out/--steps ; module entry: step()/collide_stream_bgk()/resolve_kernel_type()"}','board-audit');
